From fca6da5f264baa55c7e0d06e467d729b2f2d83da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moWerk <mo@mowerk.net>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:55:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 59/60] dt-bindings: remoteproc: qcom,glink-edge: Allow
 wakeup-source
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An incoming message on an edge, such as an SMS or call on the modem
edge, should be able to wake the system from suspend. Document the
standard wakeup-source property for the edge node.

Disclosure: LLMGD-2 · origin O1 (the model wrote it; dt_binding_check and dtbs_check for the Pro1-X dtb clean, the property used on the device by the model)
LLMGD: v0.3; assurance=A2; flags=T; origin=O1; origin_headline=O1; scope=kernel; graded-by=model; retrieval=none
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/qcom,glink-edge.yaml      | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/qcom,glink-edge.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/qcom,glink-edge.yaml
index e78a89c9e..a5fdd568e 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/qcom,glink-edge.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/qcom,glink-edge.yaml
@@ -52,6 +52,11 @@ properties:
       ID of the shared memory used by GLINK for communication with remote
       processor.
 
+  wakeup-source:
+    description:
+      An incoming message on this edge wakes the system from suspend, e.g.
+      an SMS or call arriving on the modem edge.
+
 required:
   - interrupts
   - label
-- 
